module tasks.`2026-11-27-browser-pane`

task BrowserPane {
  title "Browser pane: draw the built-in Chromium page in a pane, with input, sharing the seat's browser tools"
  verify $ make test-browser
  paths "crates/**", "Makefile", "scripts/**", "verification/**", "packaging/**", "Cargo.toml", "Cargo.lock", "ATTRIBUTION.md", "AGENTS.md", "lab/**"
  brief """
    # Browser pane

    ROLE: EXECUTOR. Operator, 2026-11-27: "implement all of this". Builds on tasks/2026-11-27-browser-over-mcp.den; do not start before that task is landed on origin/main.

    Create a goal for this task (Codex create_goal) from the outcome below and hold it until the verify command exits 0 and the change is on origin/main.

    ## Outcome

    The operator and an agent can open a browser pane in the window: the page from the built-in Chromium drawn in a pane like a seat, with mouse, scroll, keyboard and a plain address field, and the same browser the pane shows is the one browser_open, browser_cdp and browser_screenshot drive, so a person and an agent share one page.

    ## Build this

    1. Frames. The browser host renders off-screen; frames reach the window process as GPU textures (cef feature accelerated_osr: IOSurface on macOS into the existing wgpu/Metal renderer in crates/bboxy450-term), with a software-paint fallback only if the texture path cannot work, stated in the report. Frame budget and resize follow the existing pane rules.
    2. Pane kind. A browser pane opens from the GUI and through MCP (seat_spawn and seat_split accept a browser kind, or one new tool if that is fewer concepts) with a url. It has an identity the browser tools can address, closes like any pane, and survives window close and reopen the way seats do.
    3. Input. Mouse move, click, scroll, key and text input, focus, and copy and paste go to the page; the address field navigates; back, forward and reload exist.
    4. Proof. Extend make test-browser: headless --capture of a window with a browser pane showing a data: URL page, pixel-checked; a scripted click through ctl or the pane's own control changes the page and the next capture shows it; browser_cdp on the same pane reads the changed DOM. Unattended, no operator, no OS key injection, no screen capture of the desktop.
    5. Formal, words and licences as in the first task: update the lifecycle model for pane ownership (pane close, window detach, host crash while visible), the README contract and the seat skill.

    ## Rules

    Same as tasks/2026-11-27-browser-over-mcp.den. UI geometry changes run the existing parity check. Latitude: layout and chrome design are yours; keep it plain.

    ## Report

    reports/2026-11-27-browser-pane.den, then task_report with the commit on origin/main and every command with its real exit status.
    """

  managed {
    authorship = json"{\"kind\":\"seat\",\"process_generation\":\"1\",\"public_key\":\"XLMAqZTUlsEIvVxlAso8YDW5Ud3ShPEW3Kz+hD0wm1c=\",\"signer\":\"seat:01M89Z74HN4GSHEPS6TC0H6FDX\"}"
    created = json"\"2026-11-27T16:56:50.600Z\""
